<title>USA: Gillette to cut 1,700 jobs - report.</title>
<headline>Gillette to cut 1,700 jobs - report.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gillette Co will cut 1,700 jobs as part of its takeover of battery-maker Duracell International Inc, the Boston Herald reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to documents filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on Tuesday, Gillette has paid $3.3 million in severance so far and has set aside another $162.6 million for that purpose, the Herald reported.</p>
<p>As of March 31, 119 jobs have been eliminated, and most of the cuts will come from international operations and through attrition, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Gillette, which paid some $7.8 billion in stock and debt for Duracell in December, has 33,500 employees worldwide. Duracell has 9,600 workers, the Herald said..</p>
<p>Gillette officials did not return phone calls seeking comment early Wednesday morning.</p>
<p>((Boston bureau, (617)367-4106))</p>
